      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Environment \u203A Background Type decides what fills the pixels where nothing is drawn: the sky (Skybox) or one colour (Solid Color). The background is not a light: it adds nothing to the surfaces. The light of the sky comes from the Lighting window, not from the camera (see the Sky Room).\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Set Background Type to Solid Color and choose a dark blue. Will any surface in the alcove get lighter?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Set Background Type to Solid Color and pick a dark blue.\n2. Compare the walls and the floor with the background.\n3. Set the colour back to black.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: the Sky Room</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
